  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Synthesizing Contextual Data**\n\nOkay, I\'m now entering Phase 3: Plan Execution. I\'m synthesizing the three context sources. Specifically, I have \"Rumah Belajar English\" as the institution name, and I\'m noting the requested large virtual keypad for inputting the PIN, mimicking a phone keypad. Also, I\'m taking note of the user\'s focus on Fit.\n\n\n**Refining Feature Implementation**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the Iuran payment features. I\'m focusing on \"Iuran\" tab design elements such as one-click copy features for bank account numbers, and also for QRIS, and the integration of a transfer proof upload, and the use of Whatsapp to confirm payments. I\'m prioritizing user experience with a focus on ease of use.\n\n\n**Evaluating Visual Assets**\n\nI\'m now determining visual asset needs for the interface. I\'ve identified the need for a student avatar and classroom activity/worksheet images. I\'m considering using `generate_image`, or creating high-fidelity SVG/CSS representations. I\'m referring to the `frontend-design` rule for `generate_image` regarding the parallel batch generation workflow.\n\n\n**Listing Visual Assets Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing all the visual asset requests. I\'ve compiled the image generation calls, focusing on a single parallel batch turn for efficiency. I\'m focusing on the descriptions to ensure visual quality. This includes `student_avatar_kenzo`, `gallery_worksheet_handwriting`, `gallery_classroom_reading`, and `gallery_presentation_showandtell`. I am prioritizing creating high quality images, specifically to be engaging for parents and students.\n\n\n"
