  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Navigation Design**\n\nI\'m focusing on improving the tab navigation within the application. The current horizontal layout is proving too cramped. I\'m exploring a vertical, stacked menu with large, prominent buttons as a potential solution, or perhaps a bottom-anchored tab bar with oversized icons and text. My goal is to maximize usability and visual clarity.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Elderly Usability**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on accessibility for older users. The feedback regarding button size and placement is crucial. I propose a fixed bottom navigation bar with extra-large touch targets, large icons, and bold labels, maybe a vertical selector on top. Alternatively, a fixed bottom bar with `h-20` (80px), large icons, and text, with a prominent top selector. I need to get this right.\n\n\n**Evaluating Navigation Layouts**\n\nI\'m now considering a hybrid approach. The core idea involves a fixed bottom navigation bar featuring oversized icons and text, combined with large banner cards for each section. I\'m aiming for touch targets of at least 64px, bold fonts, and clear visual contrast for active states. This combined design should increase accessibility for the target demographic.\n\n\n**Adjusting Button Focus**\n\nI\'m now revising the button strategy based on recent insights. First, the size should now be a generous height (`h-20` / 80px), using bold text. Moreover, I\'m integrating vertical category buttons, situated at the top of the content, to be more readily accessible on all devices. Second, I need to remove certain buttons in `App.tsx` and `StudentProfileHeader.tsx`, streamlining the user flow, and maximizing the size of the \"Chat Miss Sarah\" button. I\'ll need to check the files to edit: `src/components/StudentProfileHeader.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Navigation Redesign**\n\nI\'m now implementing the navigation redesign in `TabNavigation.tsx`. The goal is a fixed bottom tab bar on both mobile and desktop, utilizing `fixed bottom-0 left-0 right-0 z-40 bg-white border-t-2 border-slate-300 shadow-2xl` for the layout. The target height is between 72px and 80px, incorporating large icons and bold labels for clarity. Alternatively, I\'m also considering prominent, vertically stacked buttons with a height of 60px-68px, including icons, titles, and potential badges or subtext. A prominent vertical selector with big cards at the top of the view will be tested, with stacked buttons: \"\360\237\223\213 Absensi & Catatan Guru (8 Pekan Terakhir)\", \"\360\237\216\250 Galeri Karya & Kegiatan Kelas\", and \"\360\237\222\263 Iuran Les & Konfirmasi Bayar (SPP\".\n\n\n"
