  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Admin Dashboard**\n\nI\'m currently focused on building a new admin dashboard page accessible via the /admin route, specifically for the institution owner\'s view. My priority is exclusively on two key features, aiming for a streamlined design and functionality. This means the other non-essential features are ignored for now.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Dashboard Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on two specific components for the admin dashboard. Firstly, I\'m building a \"Payment Verification Pending\" table at the top, complete with student name, class, billing month, amount, upload date, and action buttons. The action buttons will enable viewing payment proofs via a modal (using a placeholder image for now) and a \"Verify\" button to update payment status locally. Secondly, a prominent \"Upload Activity Photo\" button will initiate a modal for uploading photos with a student dropdown (using dummy data), image input, caption, and a save button that triggers a \"Photo uploaded!\" notification. I\'m aiming for a clean, desktop-friendly layout with a focus on readability and a neutral color scheme accented by green action buttons.\n\n\n**Analyzing Next Steps**\n\nI\'ve hit a point where I need to take a step back and strategize. My previous focus on the admin dashboard is complete enough to assess what\'s next. I\'m going to take a moment to evaluate.\n\n\n**Evaluating Navigation and Display**\n\nI\'m now deep in planning mode, and I\'ve started by asking some clarifying questions regarding admin dashboard navigation and display preferences. I\'ve considered how users will access the `/admin` path, favoring direct URL access with a \"Admin Mode\" link for preview. Furthermore, I\'ve assessed how to visually represent verified payments within the table, recommending a \"Lunas\" badge with the action buttons.\n\n\n"
