  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating AdminDashboard.tsx**\n\nI\'m importing `AttendanceModal`, `ClipboardCheck`, and `Link2` components, with a preference for `Link` if it\'s available. I\'ve also added a boolean state variable, `showAttendanceModal`, to manage the modal\'s visibility. This groundwork sets the stage for integrating attendance functionality directly into the admin dashboard.\n\n\n**Positioning Attendance Button**\n\nI\'ve added the \"Isi Absensi Kelas\" button, placing it beneath the \"Upload Foto Kegiatan\" button within a flex container. Its appearance and functionality are now aligned with design specifications, and the button triggers the attendance modal\'s visibility. Now I must double-check the placement logic as requested.\n\n\n**Implementing Attendance Feature**\n\nI\'m structuring the attendance input modal; a dropdown for class selection, date input, and a dummy student list with attendance status checkboxes (Present/Permission/Sick/Absent). A \"Save Attendance\" button will finalize the submission, and a toast notification confirms saving. I\'ve focused on the component placement as well. I\'m configuring the flex containers to stack \"Isi Absensi Kelas\" below \"Upload Foto Kegiatan\" on all screen sizes.\n\n\n**Refining Clipboard Functionality**\n\nI\'ve examined the `handleCopyParentLink` function and the table cell implementation. The logic determines the link and PIN to copy to the clipboard. The text is constructed dynamically based on the student\'s ID, which forms the token in the URL. I\'ve confirmed that the toast message confirms the correct name has been saved after the click.\n\n\n**Adding Verification Buttons**\n\nI\'m integrating \"Lihat Bukti\" (View Proof), \"Verifikasi\" (Verify), and \"Link Wali\" (Parent Link) buttons into the admin dashboard table. \"Lihat Bukti\" uses an eye icon; the \"Verify\" button is conditionally rendered based on payment status, green when applicable, and greyed-out when verified. Now, I\'m working to position them within the table row to enhance user experience.\n\n\n"
