  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Summary Cards**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on the summary cards for the admin page, specifically for financial insights. I plan to feature a card highlighting this month\'s total revenue (based on \"Paid\" status) and another displaying outstanding invoices. I am working to position these cards for maximum impact at the top of the admin page.\n\n\n**Refining Admin Page Design**\n\nI\'ve decided on a dedicated financial summary section at the top of the `/admin` page. I\'m imagining two prominent cards: one green, emphasizing total revenue for the month from paid invoices, and the other amber, highlighting outstanding invoices needing action. I\'m focusing on key details like bold, large numbers and visual progress indicators to grab the user\'s attention, and thinking about icons like `Wallet`, `TrendingUp`, `AlertCircle`, and `Clock`.\n\n\n**Calculating Financial Metrics**\n\nI\'m now calculating the actual financial data points for the admin dashboard. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the number of pending and verified payment records. I\'m also calculating the total income from \"lunas\" (paid) invoices. I will then utilize this information to populate the two or three summary cards. I\'m importing necessary icons from `lucide-react` to enhance the card visuals. I\'m aiming for a clear and concise presentation of key financial figures.\n\n\n**Analyzing Financial Data**\n\nI\'m now calculating pending payments and total expected income to provide context for the summary cards. I\'m also determining the collection percentage. I\'m focusing on the `payments` data to filter and reduce to get the figures I need. Then, I\'ll use those calculations to format the financial summary cards. I\'m aiming for clarity in these visualizations.\n\n\n**Presenting November\'s Earnings**\n\nI\'ve finalized the revenue card for the admin page, specifically for November 2024. The card prominently displays the total income based on \"Paid\" status, formatted as Rupiah, using the `formatRupiah` function. It also shows the number of verified invoices compared to total invoices. I\'ve chosen a green color scheme with a `Wallet` icon for easy recognition. The design is intended to be immediately informative.\n\n\n**Designing Summary Cards**\n\nI\'ve crafted the second summary card to highlight outstanding invoices. It\'s an amber-themed card displaying the number of pending invoices needing payment confirmation, alongside a \"Perlu Konfirmasi Pembayaran\" label. The design uses bold numbers and the `Clock` icon to emphasize the need for action.\n\n\n\n"
