  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Importing Key Components**\n\nI\'m in the process of importing several components into `AdminDashboard.tsx`, specifically `Wallet`, `AlertCircle`, `TrendingUp`, and `ArrowDown`. I\'m also starting to calculate some key metrics. I\'m thinking of how to display counts related to payment statuses, particularly focusing on those labeled as \"menunggu\" and \"verified\" within the `payments` data. I\'m exploring the logic for determining their counts.\n\n\n**Calculating Financial Metrics**\n\nI\'ve been working on calculating some key financial metrics based on payment statuses. I\'m focusing on \"lunas\" to determine total paid income, and \"menunggu\" to calculate total pending amounts. I\'m also finding the total billing amount, which I\'m then using to derive the collection percentage. Now I\'m shifting focus toward designing the layout of the `<main>` section for the dashboard, including an initial section for summary cards at the top.\n\n\n**Designing Summary Cards**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the summary cards for the financial overview. I\'m starting with the structure for total income this month based on the \'lunas\' status. I\'m using `TrendingUp` for a visual cue, and `CheckCircle2` for a status indicator on one card. I\'m aiming for a visually appealing layout with appropriate colors and indicators to showcase total income and billing details. The period covered is November 2024.\n\n\n**Refining Total Income Display**\n\nI\'m making final tweaks to the Total Income display card. I\'ve incorporated a visually appealing structure with bold text and appropriate color schemes. I\'m now fine-tuning the currency formatting and the overall aesthetic to make the key data standout clearly.\n\n\n**Displaying Verification Metrics**\n\nI\'m now integrating verification-related data into the dashboard\'s summary section. I\'m focusing on displaying the verified student count against the total student count. The goal is to show the collection percentage, as well as the number of payments that still require verification, using a visual layout to easily communicate payment statuses.\n\n\n**Presenting Pending Payments**\n\nI\'m now presenting pending payment data. I\'m focusing on \"waiting\" payments, displaying the count and total nominal value in a visually clear format using an `AlertCircle` icon for emphasis. I\'ve designed the display with bold numbers and appropriate color coding to highlight the \"Tagihan Siswa\" within the summary section, while formatting the rupiah values.\n\n\n**Consolidating Dashboard Summary**\n\nI\'m now consolidating the dashboard\'s summary view. The initial design included several smaller cards, but the new top summary card, which presents both total income and pending payments, effectively supersedes them. I\'m focusing on ensuring this concise overview satisfies the core requirements, making the smaller cards redundant. I am updating the `AdminDashboard.tsx` accordingly.\n\n\n"
